Cloudberry's singlenode_isolation2 tests on the port: the differences from
Cloudberry's expected output that have been reviewed, and are the port's for
a reason of its own.

Each file is a test's difference in the form ../../singlenode/canon.pl gives
it -- the lines removed and added, hunk by hunk, with no file names or line
numbers -- named for the expected output it differs from; a name with a pass
in it (test.orca.diff) holds for that pass alone.  run.sh counts a test as
passing when its difference is exactly the file's.  Both differences below
are the same in both passes.

drop_rename.diff
    Its last statement reads pg_class on every segment through
    gp_dist_random(), which arrives with M2's dispatch.  One statement; the
    three concurrent DROPs before it, which the test is about, answer as in
    Cloudberry.

pg_views_concurrent_drop.diff
    A view dropped in one session while another reads its definition from
    pg_views: Greenplum made the definition come back NULL (MPP-25160,
    try_relation_open in ruleutils.c's make_viewdef), and PostgreSQL raises
    "could not open relation with OID ...", which the test's own comment
    says.  The port runs PostgreSQL 19's ruleutils.c, which no extension can
    change, so the second session gets PostgreSQL's error.  The OID is
    masked by ../init_file.
